|While Loop|

7. Keep repeating as long as a condition is true.

count = 1
while count <= 5:
    print(count)
    count = count+1

We never increase count.
So Python sees:
1 <= 5 → True
1 <= 5 → True
1 <= 5 → True
...

It never stops.
This is called an infinite loop.
Always make sure your while condition can eventually become false.
